From 9c9b25c5573386fd8dcc906e0f17231b44e0881d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:27:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] civ45: John's decisions 9 to 12: Archery in era I, Horses, 95
 techs, a steep era curve, themed unlocks, Zealots and Alpine Troops,
 Transport 4, Residents on capture, golden ages of different kinds

Archery is an Ancient tech. Horses is a grassland and plains resource and
Horsemen, Horse Bowmen, Chariot, Zealots, Knights, Dragoons and Cavalry need one
in the city's radius. Ruler Apotheosis (the Altar), Nanomaterials (the Space
Elevator and its Tether) and Labor Union (Women's Suffrage, from Conscription)
are back: 95 advances. The era cost_pct is 100, 150, 175, 200, 225, 250, 275.
Physics unlocks the Siege Workshop (Veteran_Build for siege units), Medicine the
Apothecary (Health_Pct 30, HP_Regen 10 for land units), Electricity the
Telegraph Office (one trade route). Alpine Troops return at Tactics (14, IgTer,
Gun) and Crusaders return as Zealots (Monotheism, 8, move 2, Horses, no Iron).
The Transport carries 4. script.lua records each settled great person's kind per
city and re-creates the Residents on city_transferred and, for trades and
incitement, when the owner no longer matches at turn start. A golden age needs
great people of different kinds, one more than the last: a pledge raises a
"Pledge of the <Kind>" small wonder in the capital that the kind's enabler
reads, and the age removes them; the AI pledges one of each kind it lacks.
