index adfafdc..3fa22ab 100644
--- a/data/civ45/README.civ45
+++ b/data/civ45/README.civ45
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@ Differences from sandbox
   the whip too: disbanded in a city ("Disband recovering production")
   each puts 30 shields into the build, whatever it cost, so a citizen
   becomes 30 shields. No unhappiness follows a draft yet.
-- The roster: 76 unit types over seven eras (notes/freeciv45/design/
+- The roster: 78 unit types over seven eras (notes/freeciv45/design/
   units-and-upgrades.md), with one strength number for attack and
   defence (0 attack for scouts, transports, machine gunners, air
   defence and the radar plane), 10 hit points in the first three eras,
@@ -93,7 +93,9 @@ Differences from sandbox
   Mech. Inf. Mechanized Infantry, Helicopter Gunship, AWACS Radar Plane,
   AEGIS Cruiser Missile Cruiser, SSBN Missile Submarine, ICBM Nuclear
   Missile), so saves and scripts load. Jaguar Warrior, Immortal, Alpine
-  Troops, Crusaders and Mechanic are gone (Engineers heal vehicles).
+  Troops, Crusaders and Mechanic are gone (Engineers heal vehicles);
+  Alpine Troops are back at Tactics and Zealots (mounted, Monotheism,
+  no armour) stand where Crusaders stood. Transports carry four.
 - Great people (notes/freeciv45/design/great-people.md): every city
   collects great-person points from its temples, libraries, markets,
   theatres, courts and their successors (1 to 3 a turn), from wonders
@@ -106,15 +108,16 @@ Differences from sandbox
   (a free tech, 240 shields into a wonder, a trade mission, 400 history,
   the Sanctum, a veteran level for the stack, or the diplomat actions)
   or pledges a golden age: ten turns of +1 shield and +1 trade on
-  working tiles, double points and no anarchy, for one pledge, then two,
-  then three. The first to Philosophy, Theology, Economics or
+  working tiles, double points and no anarchy, for one pledge, then two
+  of different kinds, then three. A captured city keeps its Residents. The first to Philosophy, Theology, Economics or
   Electricity gets one free. script.lua runs it, and spends the AI's
   great people for it each turn through the same actions.
 - Strategic resources: Swordsmen, Macebearers, Crossbowmen, Knights,
   Cannon, Ship of the Line and Ironclad need Iron (Ironclad Coal too),
   War Elephants Ivory, and armour, aircraft and modern warships Oil,
-  somewhere in the city's radius. Horses, copper, aluminium and uranium
-  wait for the resources slice.
+  somewhere in the city's radius, and every mounted unit from Horsemen
+  to Cavalry needs Horses (a grassland and plains resource). Copper,
+  aluminium and uranium wait for the resources slice.
 - Nation-unique buildings: Arab Bazaar (built on a Marketplace, +50%
   luxury, +25% gold). No new graphics yet; they reuse the sprites of the
   unit or building they replace.
